 "patent_text": "At the same retransmission budget, the soft-syndrome guard reduced the number of undetected frame errors of the neural decoder by 48 % on the AWGN channel and 50 % on the burst channel relative to the conventional minimum-|LLR| threshold test, and by 52 % / 53 % relative to plain CRC acceptance. Applied unchanged to a classical Hamming(7,4) soft decoder it reduced undetected errors by 80 % (AWGN) and 49 % (burst), demonstrating that the guard is independent of the decoder. Because both gates were held to the same retransmission budget, the ARQ goodput of the guarded link stayed within about 1 % of the unguarded link from 3 dB upward, the usable operating range, and within a few percent at 0-2 dB, where goodput is already very low. Replacing the analytic risk by a learned gradient-boosted risk classifier built on the same inputs lowered the undetected count by a further 56 % (AWGN) and 24 % (burst) at the same retransmission budget."
